1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,664
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,664 --> 00:00:03,640
OTTO: Hey! That's not fair!

3
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,057
Is this really half?

4
00:00:06,657 --> 00:00:09,842
Today's case: what is a half?

5
00:00:10,242 --> 00:00:14,884
Half means two pieces. Both pieces are the same size.

6
00:00:15,984 --> 00:00:21,225
Like a lamington for two friends. Each friend gets the same.

7
00:00:22,325 --> 00:00:26,247
OTTO: One ribbon, two kites. I'll cut it right here!

8
00:00:26,647 --> 00:00:29,138
IVY: Wait. Is that the middle?

9
00:00:29,747 --> 00:00:36,047
The mark might not be in the middle. Then one piece is longer.

10
00:00:37,147 --> 00:00:39,749
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

11
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:42,669
A. At Otto's mark.

12
00:00:42,869 --> 00:00:45,751
B. Somewhere else.

13
00:00:45,951 --> 00:00:48,322
Pause and think.

14
00:00:53,322 --> 00:00:55,714
BRAMBLE: Can you point to the middle?

15
00:00:59,714 --> 00:01:04,514
Watch the ends. Bring one end to meet the other.

16
00:01:05,114 --> 00:01:06,500
BRAMBLE: Ends together.

17
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:12,327
The two ends match. So both sides are the same length.

18
00:01:13,427 --> 00:01:16,319
The fold shows the middle.

19
00:01:17,419 --> 00:01:22,711
The middle is here. Otto's mark is over there. It's B!

20
00:01:23,111 --> 00:01:25,850
OTTO: Oops. My mark was too far.

21
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:28,851
Cut at the fold.

22
00:01:29,251 --> 00:01:30,972
Line them up.

23
00:01:32,051 --> 00:01:35,658
Ten centimetres, and ten centimetres.

24
00:01:36,058 --> 00:01:37,452
Same length!

25
00:01:37,852 --> 00:01:39,348
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

26
00:01:40,748 --> 00:01:42,112
IVY: They match!

27
00:01:42,512 --> 00:01:48,186
Two equal pieces. Equal means the same. Each one is a half.

28
00:01:48,786 --> 00:01:49,603
OTTO: Yay!

29
00:01:49,803 --> 00:01:52,936
OTTO: Oops! Who turned off the lights?

30
00:01:53,936 --> 00:01:56,580
Remember. Say it with me.

31
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,125
Half means...

32
00:01:59,925 --> 00:02:02,034
two equal parts!

33
00:02:03,134 --> 00:02:07,610
To find the middle, fold it end to end.

34
00:02:08,710 --> 00:02:12,633
Try it at home. Use string or paper.

35
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:17,201
Next case: four pieces. Are they fair?

